# NoX release key (ssh-keygen allowed-signers format, one per line):
#   <principal> namespaces="<list>" ssh-ed25519 AAAA…
# It verifies what the maintainer signs at a release:
#   - the annotated git tag vX.Y.Z (signature namespace "git"):
#       git -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=release/allowed-signers verify-tag vX.Y.Z
#   - SHA256SUMS of the release ISO (namespace "nox-release"):
#       ssh-keygen -Y verify -f release/allowed-signers -I nox-release \
#         -n nox-release -s SHA256SUMS.sig < SHA256SUMS
# A key inside the repo proves nothing by itself: compare its fingerprint
# (ssh-keygen -lf nox-release.pub) with the one published outside the repo.
# See docs/release.md. The maintainer fills in the line below (public key
# of nox-release, never a private one) and removes the comment mark.
#nox-release namespaces="git,nox-release" ssh-ed25519 AAAA…
